body:
This may need to be a separate function. It does not make sense for scitools to re-create its database every time. What you may create multiple times is the XML file out of the DB. Did you try running the tool manually to get the Class and the File XML out of it? Did creating one DB suffice to them use the other commands to extract the XML files? 

If anything, I worry that having the DB here will mean the second function call will fail. 

@crepesAlot note this is a new tool that has to appear in the project configuration file. Did you coordinate?

Add a help block for both build and parse. See the preexisting exec files for examples, but it would look something like this:
```
if (arguments[["build"]] & arguments[["help"]]) {
  cli::cli_alert_info("some useful message for what build does.")
} else if (arguments[["parse"]]) {
//parse logic
```
